69- We also evaluate a simpler method where we create unit tests for the Java functions in the test dataset and use them to reorder the elements of the beam at test time. We compute the results of the tests for every proposed C++ or Python translation and prioritize the elements that pass the unit tests. As shown on Table 6 reordering the elements of the beam at test time when translating from Java leads only to small improvements compared to the best baseline (up to 1.7% CA@1 for Java → Python) and the scores of this method are far from those obtained when requiring any of the 10 element of the beam to be correct (i e. CA@10). It can be explained by the fact that the tests generated by EvoSuite on these functions can have low mutation scores and be insufﬁcient to thor- oughly test the semantics of the functions. Moreover, the tests we create are sometimes incompatible with those of our test set (see Figure 4 for an example) 19
